{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00318",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 5.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Hi, doctor. Long queue outside, but here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.36,
      "end_seconds": 12.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.54,
      "end_seconds": 18.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, honestly, it's constipation, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.72,
      "end_seconds": 24.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "And when did that start? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.79,
      "end_seconds": 31.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "I've had it for four weeks. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.9,
      "end_seconds": 38.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "And what do you do to cope with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.74,
      "end_seconds": 44.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Drinking more water helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.35,
      "end_seconds": 52.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Um, um, I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 52.57,
      "end_seconds": 58.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.43,
      "end_seconds": 60.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.76,
      "end_seconds": 73.97,
      "duration_seconds": 13.21,
      "text": "Oh, and a heavy feeling in the lower tummy. That's been about the same, two months. Oh, and a little bright blood on the paper. That's been about the same, six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.34,
      "end_seconds": 77.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Has there been any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.73,
      "end_seconds": 79.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "No, no weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.43,
      "end_seconds": 85.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any vomiting, black stools, abdominal swelling or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.04,
      "end_seconds": 98.1,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "No, no vomiting, no black stools, no abdominal swelling. I did have straining to pass stool at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.83,
      "end_seconds": 100.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.29,
      "end_seconds": 103.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Right, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.19,
      "end_seconds": 109.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Right, moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.26,
      "end_seconds": 125.54,
      "duration_seconds": 15.28,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I did try to ignore it for a while. I have an underactive thyroid, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.25,
      "end_seconds": 135.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Go on. Right, so that's your known diabetes. We'll keep that in mind today. Okay, I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.76,
      "end_seconds": 139.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Um, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.98,
      "end_seconds": 142.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.26,
      "end_seconds": 146.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Okay, so my mother has diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.59,
      "end_seconds": 150.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.72,
      "end_seconds": 151.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.2,
      "end_seconds": 165.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Alright, are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.78,
      "end_seconds": 170.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 171.57,
      "end_seconds": 175.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 250 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.05,
      "end_seconds": 180.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.59,
      "end_seconds": 188.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.81,
      "text": "Well, I don't think I have it with me. Thyroxine, 75 micrograms, maybe, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.16,
      "end_seconds": 196.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Okay, did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.78,
      "end_seconds": 208.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.71,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. It's, It's Cremaffin, at night. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.97,
      "end_seconds": 213.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.74,
      "end_seconds": 216.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "So, yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.2,
      "end_seconds": 224.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "So, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.04,
      "end_seconds": 234.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.5,
      "text": "Oh, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.93,
      "end_seconds": 240.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "So, is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.83,
      "end_seconds": 245.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 245.97,
      "end_seconds": 251.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse 69, saturation 99 percent, BP is 122 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.98,
      "end_seconds": 253.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.27,
      "end_seconds": 258.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.44,
      "end_seconds": 262.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.98,
      "end_seconds": 281.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "There's no mass in the tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.71,
      "end_seconds": 284.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.96,
      "end_seconds": 298.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "I can feel firm stool in the left lower abdomen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.82,
      "end_seconds": 300.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.36,
      "end_seconds": 309.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.94,
      "end_seconds": 313.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.05,
      "end_seconds": 314.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.21,
      "end_seconds": 346.26,
      "duration_seconds": 16.05,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with chronic constipation at this stage. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep haemorrhoids in mind. I can't rule out an underactive thyroid yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.99,
      "end_seconds": 349.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Uh, doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.45,
      "end_seconds": 365.49,
      "duration_seconds": 14.04,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now chronic constipation is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had constipation for four weeks, and no weight loss or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.46,
      "end_seconds": 368.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.33,
      "end_seconds": 373.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.83,
      "end_seconds": 374.53,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.2,
      "end_seconds": 391.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Let's get a colonoscopy, for constipation and rectal bleeding. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 394.27,
      "end_seconds": 397.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "I can book that for Tuesday at 3:30 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.99,
      "end_seconds": 398.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.49,
      "end_seconds": 413.83,
      "duration_seconds": 14.34,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for constipation. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'm prescribing lactulose, 15 ml, at night, for two weeks. It's for constipation. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.58,
      "end_seconds": 417.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 418.95,
      "end_seconds": 442.98,
      "duration_seconds": 24.03,
      "text": "More fibre, more water, and give yourself ten unhurried minutes after breakfast. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 443.83,
      "end_seconds": 445.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 446.3,
      "end_seconds": 452.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 453.61,
      "end_seconds": 456.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "So, uh, yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 457.72,
      "end_seconds": 460.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 461.24,
      "end_seconds": 461.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 462.51,
      "end_seconds": 466.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 470.74,
      "end_seconds": 478.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "So, I take the lactulose, 15 ml, at night and come back in a month. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 480.51,
      "end_seconds": 484.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 485.89,
      "end_seconds": 488.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Right, thanks so much, doctor."
    }
  ]
}